{"id":"74ef97b7-fa2d-487a-9533-f91442112380","object":"chat.completion","created":1785033415,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    \\n    edges = []\\n    for a, b, d in distances:\\n        w = max(core[a], core[b], d)\\n        if a > b:\\n            a, b = b, a\\n        edges.append((w, a, b))\\n    \\n    edges.sort()\\n    \\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\\n    \\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    \\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    \\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    target = len(nodes) - 1\\n    for w, a, b in edges:\\n        if union(a, b):\\n            mst_edges.append([a, b, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == target:\\n                break\\n    \\n    return {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to generate a Python implementation for `solve(case)` that computes a Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) using mutual reachability distances as defined in HDBSCAN. The payload contains `nodes`, `core_distance` dict, and `distances` list of [node1, node2, distance]. We need to compute mutual reachability = max(core_dist[node1], core_dist[node2], distance). Then we need to construct a full graph with all pairs? Actually, the distances list may not be complete; it likely includes all pairs given the fixture. But we sho